extraction_notes: |
  - Pages: heading and lore printed 57, special powers printed 58, powers 4-8 and the stat block printed 59 (cache p058-p060). The text layer was clean for these pages; nothing needed a render. "LS.P."/"xlO" digit faults read as I.S.P./x10.
  - GROUP: the book heads it an R.C.C. but it is stored as category occ, occ_group psychic, per this batch''s Mind Melter convention. No S.D.C. or hit point formula is printed, so men_of_arms: false (a psychic, not a man of arms).
  - XP: xp_table is the Nega-Psychic ladder read off printed 157.
  - I.S.P.: 2D4x10 + M.E., only +2D4 per level (not the usual +10); considered a Master Psychic, so saves vs psionics on 10 or higher (from psionics.type). Stored as prose isp_base.
  - P.P.E.: P.E. x2 +1D6 per level, stored as prose ppe_base. The book adds that Psi-Stalkers and other P.P.E.-sensitive beings cannot detect the Nega-Psychic''s P.P.E., and that it is not used to cast magic; that is in Closed to the Supernatural / GM Notes, not a field.
  - PSIONICS: five automatic powers granted by name (Exorcism, Suppress Fear, Deaden Senses, Summon Inner Strength, Group Mind Block; Group Mind Block is a Super catalog row, granted outright). Mind Block is NOT granted as a power: the book says the character is closed "as if" a Mind Block were constantly in force at no cost, which is a special ability. One Physical pick at level 1 (powers_starting 1) and one at 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 14 (powers_schedule).
  - BONUSES: +2 vs mind control (the book adds "including drugs"; stored as mind_control only, harmful_drugs NOT raised because the line means mind-control drugs), +2 vs poison and disease (toxins_poisons, disease), +2 vs magic illusions (illusionary_magic), +1 vs Horror Factor at levels 1, 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15, +1 vs magic spells and rituals at 3, 7 and 13 (spell_magic and ritual_magic). Combat +1 initiative, +1 parry, +2 dodge, +1 disarm, +2 pull punch, +1 roll with impact. Imperviousness to possession, potions, curses, magic illnesses and Psychosomatic Disease is not a number and is in special_abilities.
  - SKILLS: Speaks Native tongue at 98 plus one Language: Other +30%. "Literate in one language of choice (+15%)" is a pick between Literacy: Native Language and Literacy: Other. Basic & Advanced Math +15% is Mathematics: Basic 45+15 and Mathematics: Advanced 45+15. Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+15. Lore: one of choice (+10%) enumerates the catalog''s Rifts-relevant Lore rows other than Demons & Monsters (Nightbane-system lores left out). Wilderness Survival 30+10, Land Navigation 36+10. Technical two of choice (+15%). W.P. Energy Rifle plus one W.P. of choice.
  - HAND TO HAND: none is granted; the book says it must be taken as an R.C.C. Related skill at Basic 1 pick, Expert 2, Martial Arts (or Assassin if evil) 3. Stored as the hand_to_hand cost block with basic priced.
  - RELATED: eight, plus one at 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15. Category bonuses as printed. Piloting Any (+10%) is Pilot; Horsemanship is also offered at +10% because the catalog files riding skills under their own category (judgement call, following the Amazon import). Cowboy: None is omitted. Secondary: four, plus two at 3, 6, 9 and 12, base only.
  - EQUIPMENT: "M.D.C. body armor of choice" enumerates common catalog armors. "Silver cross" is a pick between the small and large silver cross rows (size not printed). Air filter AND gas mask are both given, as printed. "Tape recorder" is mapped to the Rifts pocket-digital-disc-recorder row (judgement call; a Heroes Unlimited tape-recorder row also exists). Lighter is disposable-lighter. 50 feet of lightweight cord is the lightweight-cord row (a 50 ft bundle). "Energy rifle of choice (excluding CS rifles)" enumerates non-CS catalog rifles. The "weapon of choice" is not enumerated - it follows the W.P. of choice pick; GM to supply. The vehicle is a battered hovercycle or Land Rover of choice with M.D.C. reduced by 4D6%; the catalog has no Land Rover, so jeep stands in, and the M.D.C. reduction is prose only.
  - BOOK TENSION: power 6 (printed 59) halves the penalties and duration of magic-induced illnesses, disorders and curses, while power 8 on the same page makes the character impervious to magic curses and magic illnesses. Both are recorded as printed; read together, the halving applies to magic-induced disorders the imperviousness does not cover. GM call.
  - MONEY: 2D6x100 Universal credits stored; the 2D4x100 in tradeable goods is not coin and is not stored.
  - NOT STORED: Race restrictions (humans 70%, Ogres 12%, Elves 10%, Psi-Stalkers 5%, others 3%; 65% male) and the alignment tendency (none, leans good, unprincipled or aberrant). A high M.A. and P.S. are helpful but not required. Cybernetics: starts with none and avoids augmentation (a restriction line).
---

## Lore

Before the Great Cataclysm, a Nega-Psychic was a psychic who flatly refused to believe in magic or the paranormal, and that stubborn disbelief shaped his own hidden psionics into a shield against the very things he denied. On Rifts Earth, where demons, dragons and sorcery are everyday facts, the modern Nega-Psychic accepts that such forces exist but refuses to let them rule, harm or dominate him. He is a defiant, strong-willed rebel and a natural enemy of the supernatural beings, sorcerers, psychics and tyrants who treat humans as lesser creatures. Many are near-fanatical about personal freedom and the value of human life, and their powers leave them all but immune to mind control and possession.

## GM Notes

**Closed to the Supernatural** works like a permanent, free Mind Block. It cuts both ways: the character cannot sense supernatural evil or magic, and nothing psychic or magical senses him. To other psychics he is a blank slate. Telepathy and empathy cannot reach him unless he deliberately opens himself, which is rare because being closed is the root of his defenses. His P.P.E. is likewise invisible to Psi-Stalkers and other P.P.E.-sensitive beings, and he does not use it to cast magic.

**Disrupt Magic** is an active countermeasure: the Nega-Psychic spends P.P.E. at a 1:3 ratio against a spell or ritual being cast within 10 ft + 5 ft per level. A spell left short of its cost fails and the caster''s P.P.E. is lost either way. A caster who knows what he faces can over-spend by three or more, and the Nega-Psychic can anticipate that and spend in increments of three - a battle of wits the GM can play out round by round. Unlike the Psi-Nullifier, the Nega-Psychic cannot disrupt psionics, though he resists many of them.

**Imperviousness:** immune to possession, all Mind Bleeder powers, magic potions (even helpful ones), magic curses and magic illnesses, and the psionic power Psychosomatic Disease. Magic-induced illnesses and disorders he does suffer run at half penalty and duration, and he heals twice as fast as a normal human.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nega-psychic');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nega-psychic';

